P0002 Early Hints on a pushed response causes a library panic


P0003    [src/proto/streams/state.rs:162](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/state.rs:162), [src/proto/streams/recv.rs:171](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/recv.rs:171).


P0004    Expected: a pushed response may send `103 Early Hints` before its final response.


P0005    Observed: receiving 103 leaves the stream in `ReservedRemote`, although it has already been counted. The final response counts it again and panics at `src/proto/streams/counts.rs:111`: `assertion failed: !stream.is_counted`.


P0006    Consequence: an ordinary client connection task panics while processing a valid response sequence.


P0007    Evidence: executed `pushed_get_accepts_early_hints_before_final_response`, using a promised GET followed by 103 and 200. Source inspection confirms the assertion is unconditional.


P0008    transition out of the reserved state on the first response HEADERS while continuing to await final headers; count the stream once.


P0009 Discarded DATA padding is omitted from flow control


P0010    [src/proto/streams/recv.rs:580](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/recv.rs:580).


P0011    Expected: DATA flow control accounts for the entire frame payload, including padding and its length byte. Discarded padding capacity must become reusable.


P0012    Observed: accounting uses only the body length after padding has been stripped.


P0013    Consequence: a conforming peer can exhaust its window and stall, even after the application consumes and releases all body data.


P0014    Evidence: executed `padded_data_returns_discarded_padding_capacity`. A 16-byte stream window was filled with one body byte, one padding-length byte, and fourteen padding bytes. After releasing the body byte, no WINDOW_UPDATE arrived within 100 ms. The equivalent unpadded control passed. Source inspection confirms padding never reaches the receive accounting.


P0015    account for all flow-controlled octets and automatically release discarded padding at both stream and connection levels.


P0016 Reading an empty body consumes and loses its trailing headers. src/proto/streams/recv.rs:1116. When a response consists of initial HEADERS followed directly by trailing HEADERS with END_STREAM, RecvStream::data() pops the next receive event while looking for DATA. Its non-DATA branch returns None and consumes the trailer event. Consequently a normal caller that finishes the body loop before calling trailers() gets Ok(None), losing application metadata such as x-result: ok on responses that contain no DATA frames.


P0017 A valid 304 response fails when ended with empty DATA


P0018    [src/proto/streams/recv.rs:187](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/recv.rs:187), [src/proto/streams/recv.rs:641](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/recv.rs:641).


P0019    Expected: a 304 response may carry a representation `Content-Length` without sending that content, including when an empty DATA frame ends the stream.


P0020    Observed: the length is retained as outstanding body data; the empty final DATA frame produces `PROTOCOL_ERROR`.


P0021    Consequence: an ordinary conditional GET can fail depending on how the server terminates its response.


P0022    Evidence: executed `not_modified_accepts_empty_end_data` with status 304, `Content-Length: 100`, and empty final DATA. It failed. Ending the same response in HEADERS passed.


P0023    represent 304’s no-content semantics throughout body validation, rather than exempting only END_STREAM HEADERS.


P0024 A 4 GiB capacity request silently becomes zero


P0025    [src/share.rs:287](/work/crate/src/share.rs:287).


P0026    Expected: `reserve_capacity(usize)` preserves a positive request or applies a documented limit.


P0027    Observed: casting to `WindowSize` truncates the argument. On this 64-bit host, `reserve_capacity(1usize << 32)` becomes `reserve_capacity(0)`.


P0028    Consequence: an uploader reserving its remaining file size can cancel its reservation and wait indefinitely for capacity.


P0029    Evidence: executed `reserve_large_body_does_not_cancel_reservation`. An existing positive reservation became zero. Controls requesting 65,535 bytes, 2 GiB, and 4 GiB minus one retained available capacity.


P0030    clamp before conversion or use a checked conversion with a documented policy for large requests.


P0031 Pushed HEAD responses reject valid representation lengths


P0032    [src/proto/streams/recv.rs:749](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/recv.rs:749).


P0033    Expected: pushed HEAD responses receive the same no-body treatment as directly requested HEAD responses. The crate explicitly permits HEAD promises.


P0034    Observed: promise processing never sets `ContentLength::Head`. A 200 response with `Content-Length: 100` and END_STREAM is rejected with `PROTOCOL_ERROR`.


P0035    Consequence: clients cannot receive otherwise valid pushed HEAD metadata.


P0036    Evidence: executed `pushed_head_accepts_representation_content_length`. Controls using a directly requested HEAD, or a pushed HEAD with length zero, passed.


